{"name":"Dr. White","hex":"#fafafa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dr.","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Dr (debitor)","Abbreviation of drachm (“dram”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dr."},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Doctor (title)","blocks":[{"text":"Doctor is an academic title that originates from the Latin word of the same spelling. The word is originally an agentive noun of the Latin verb docēre 'to teach' and thus translates directly to teacher. It has been used as an academic title in Europe since the 13th century, when the first doctorates were awarded at the University of Bologna and the University of Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aquatint_of_a_Doctor_in_divinity_at_the_University_of_Oxford%2C_shown_wearing_convocation_dress.jpg/330px-Aquatint_of_a_Doctor_in_divinity_at_the_University_of_Oxford%2C_shown_wearing_convocation_dress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_(title)"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg/500px-Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg/1280px-Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg/500px-Ancient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_%2828661031841%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Ancient Greek Marble Consecration Relief to a Heroic Doctor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAncient_Greek_Marble_Consecration_Relief_to_a_Heroic_Doctor%2C_c._50_BC_to_50_AD_(28661031841).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/The_Union_Minister_for_Health_%26_Family_Welfare%2C_Shri_J.P._Nadda_presenting_the_Phd_degree_to_a_student_at_the_20th_Convocation_Ceremony_of_NIMHANS%2C_at_Bengaluru_on_February_13%2C_2016.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/The_Union_Minister_for_Health_%2